    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40866" root="هت" body-key="h">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَهْتُوتٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَتِيتٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الهَمْزَةُ صَوْتٌ مَهْتُوتٌ فِى</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَقْصَى الحَلْقِ</span> [<i>Hemzeh is a sound uttered</i> (after
a suppression of the breath) <i>in the most remote
part of the throat</i>]. (Kh, L.) Sb applied the
term <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَهْتُوتُ</span> to the letter <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ه</span>, because of its weakness and lowness. (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسْرَعُ مِنَ المُهَتْهِتَةِ</span>
<i>Quicker than the quick-speaking woman.</i> (IAar.)

